2. Criteo Uplift Modeling Dataset v2.1 - separate data license

Dataset: Criteo Uplift Modeling Dataset, corrected release v2.1
Provider: Criteo / Criteo AI Lab
Archive: criteo-research-uplift-v2.1.csv.gz
License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0
         International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)
SPDX identifier: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0

Historical licensing note: the datasheet appendix in the 2021 benchmark paper
describes the dataset as CC BY-SA 4.0. This project follows the more restrictive
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 license identified by Criteo's official hosting page, consistent
with DATA_CARD.md. Obtain clarification from Criteo before relying on a
different interpretation.

Official dataset page and data terms:
https://ailab.criteo.com/criteo-uplift-prediction-dataset/

Official dataset card and download:
https://huggingface.co/datasets/criteo/criteo-uplift

License summary:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

Full legal terms:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode.en

The project author does not own or relicense the Criteo dataset. The MIT
License in section 1 does not grant permission to use the dataset commercially
or remove any conditions imposed by its data license.

When exercising rights under the data license, including sharing the dataset
or sharing adapted material, comply with the full legal terms. In particular:

- Attribution: give appropriate credit to Criteo, retain supplied attribution
  and license notices, link to the license and source, and indicate changes.
  Do not imply that Criteo endorses this project or its results.
- NonCommercial: use of the licensed dataset and adapted material under this
  license must be noncommercial. Commercial use requires separate permission
  from the relevant rights holder.
- ShareAlike: when sharing adapted material, apply CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 or an
  adapter's license permitted by its ShareAlike provisions.
- No additional restrictions: do not impose legal terms or technological
  measures that restrict recipients from exercising the licensed rights.

These conditions apply to raw data and to processed data, subsets, or other
outputs to the extent they constitute licensed material or adapted material.
They do not automatically relicense independently authored analysis code.
Applicable exceptions and limitations remain available under the full terms.

Repository distribution policy: this project does not commit or redistribute
raw, extracted, or processed row-level Criteo data, including extracted CSV
files, Parquet copies, row-level samples, and other transformed row-level
copies. It distributes only documentation, download and processing code,
checksums, analytical code, and non-row-level results. Users must obtain the
dataset directly from Criteo's official source and comply with its data
license. This is the project's distribution policy; it does not impose
additional restrictions on rights granted by the original data license.

This section is a notice and summary, not a replacement for the full data
license. The dataset is supplied without warranties under that license.

3. Dataset attribution and citation

Criteo AI Lab. Criteo Uplift Modeling Dataset, corrected release v2.1.
Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/criteo/criteo-uplift
License: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
Any redistributed adaptation must additionally describe the changes made.

The dataset provider requests citation of the original release. Consistent
with DATA_CARD.md, this project cites both the original release and the later
corrected-dataset benchmark:

Eustache Diemert, Artem Betlei, Christophe Renaudin, and Massih-Reza Amini.
2018. A Large Scale Benchmark for Uplift Modeling.
Proceedings of the AdKDD and TargetAd Workshop, KDD, London, United Kingdom,
August 20, 2018.
https://www.adkdd.org/papers/a-large-scale-benchmark-for-uplift-modeling/2018

Diemert, E., Betlei, A., Renaudin, C., Amini, M.-R., Gregoir, T., and
Rahier, T. 2021.
A Large Scale Benchmark for Individual Treatment Effect Prediction and
Uplift Modeling. arXiv:2111.10106.
https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.10106

